<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xhosa people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as amaXhosa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xhosa are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, speaking isiXhosa. In the late eighteenth and nineteenth centuries they fought a long series of frontier wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, lost much of their land and suffered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-killing movement of 1856–1857. Prominent Xhosa include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>, and the language is spoken by some eight million people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xhosa-people.jpg" alt="Xhosa people" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archives anon. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zonnebloem_College_-_Xhosa_graduates_-_Cape_Town_Cape_Colony_1860.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
